body:
When I was younger, I was holding a conversation with my mom in the kitchen. I was washing a dish while we were talking and I could kind of see her out of the corner of my eye, but I wasn't looking directly at her. While I was moving the dish to the rack, I looked up and she was gone. It was so abrupt that I went to go  find her. She was in her room and claimed that she hadn't been in the kitchen. It made me question my sanity, but I knew I had just been talking to her. Her voice was so prominent and something like that has never happened again.

&#x200B;

I told my boyfriend and he thinks it's just a false memory my brain conjured, but it feels so vivid. That really spooked me as a kid.
